        "content": "\n`requireReviewer()` / `getReviewer()` wrap Clerk's `auth()`/`currentUser()`. Needs `vi.mock(\"@clerk/nextjs/server\")`.\n\n**Gaps:** unauthenticated throw path, authenticated-but-`currentUser()` returns null, label derivation delegation to `reviewerLabel`.\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/auth.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\nimport { requireReviewer, getReviewer } from \"./auth\";\nimport { auth, currentUser } from \"@clerk/nextjs/server\";\n\nvi.mock(\"@clerk/nextjs/server\", () => ({\n  auth: vi.fn(),\n  currentUser: vi.fn(),\n}));\n\ndescribe(\"requireReviewer\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => vi.resetAllMocks());\n\n  it(\"throws when isAuthenticated is false\", async () => {\n    (auth as any).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: false, userId: null });\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).rejects.toThrow(/No authenticated reviewer/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws when isAuthenticated is true but userId is missing (inconsistent session)\", async () => {\n    (auth as any).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: null });\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).rejects.toThrow();\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns userId and derived label when authenticated\", async () => {\n    (auth as any).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: \"u_1\" });\n    (currentUser as any).mockResolvedValue({ username: \"j.rao\", primaryEmailAddress: null });\n    const reviewer = await requireReviewer();\n    expect(reviewer).toEqual({ userId: \"u_1\", label: \"j.rao\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"falls back to userId as label when currentUser has no username/email\", async () => {\n    (auth as any).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: \"u_2\" });\n    (currentUser as any).mockResolvedValue(null);\n    const reviewer = await requireReviewer();\n    expect(reviewer.label).toBe(\"u_2\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"getReviewer\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => vi.resetAllMocks());\n\n  it(\"returns null when signed out (does not throw)\", async () => {\n    (auth as any).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: false, userId: null });\n    await expect(getReviewer()).resolves.toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it(\"delegates to requireReviewer when signed in\", async () => {\n    (auth as any).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: \"u_3\" });\n    (currentUser as any).mockResolvedValue({ username: \"a\", primaryEmailAddress: null });\n    await expect(getReviewer()).resolves.toEqual({ userId: \"u_3\", label: \"a\" });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "3. Data access — `lib/server/sources.ts`",
        "content": "\nCurrently entirely untested; `countSourcesBySide` has a subtle bug surface: `synthetic` sources aren't counted in `crm` or `warehouse`, which the UI may assume is exhaustive.\n\n**Gaps:** empty source list, mixed kinds, `sourceSchema.parse` throwing on a malformed DB row (schema drift), ordering by `createdAt` is delegated to the DB and untestable without an integration test.\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/sources.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport { listSources, countSourcesBySide } from \"./sources\";\nimport { getDb } from \"@/lib/db\";\n\nvi.mock(\"next/server\", () => ({ connection: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(undefined) }));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/db\", () => ({ getDb: vi.fn() }));\n\nfunction mockRows(rows: unknown[]) {\n  (getDb as any).mockReturnValue({\n    select: () => ({ from: () => ({ orderBy: () => Promise.resolve(rows) }) }),\n  });\n}\n\ndescribe(\"listSources\", () => {\n  it(\"returns an empty array when there are no rows\", async () => {\n    mockRows([]);\n    await expect(listSources()).resolves.toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  it(\"parses valid rows into Source objects\", async () => {\n    mockRows([{\n      id: \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\",\n      name: \"SFDC prod\", kind: \"salesforce\",\n      config: { objects: [\"Account\"] },\n      createdAt: new Date(\"2026-01-01\"),\n    }]);\n    const result = await listSources();\n    expect(result).toHaveLength(1);\n    expect(result[0].name).toBe(\"SFDC prod\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws when a row fails schema validation (e.g. bad kind from DB drift)\", async () => {\n    mockRows([{ id: \"x\", name: \"bad\", kind: \"not-a-kind\", config: {}, createdAt: new Date() }]);\n    await expect(listSources()).rejects.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"countSourcesBySide\", () => {\n  it(\"buckets salesforce/hubspot as crm, databricks/snowflake as warehouse, synthetic separately\", async () => {\n    mockRows([\n      { id: \"1\", name: \"a\", kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] }, createdAt: new Date() },\n      { id: \"2\", name: \"b\", kind: \"hubspot\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] }, createdAt: new Date() },\n      { id: \"3\", name: \"c\", kind: \"databricks\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] }, createdAt: new Date() },\n      { id: \"4\", name: \"d\", kind: \"synthetic\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] }, createdAt: new Date() },\n    ]);\n    await expect(countSourcesBySide()).resolves.toEqual({ crm: 2, warehouse: 1, synthetic: 1 });\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns all-zero counts for an empty source list\", async () => {\n    mockRows([]);\n    await expect(countSourcesBySide()).resolves.toEqual({ crm: 0, warehouse: 0, synthetic: 0 });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "4. Zod schemas — `types/*.ts` (no tests currently validate the contracts these mirror `engine/pipeline/schema.py`)",
        "content": "\nThese are the \"tool contract\" boundary — if the engine and web schemas drift, failures happen silently at parse time in prod. Worth round-trip tests.\n\n```ts\n// types/source.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { createSourceSchema, sourceConfigSchema } from \"./source\";\n\ndescribe(\"createSourceSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"accepts a minimal valid source\", () => {\n    expect(createSourceSchema.safeParse({\n      name: \"A\", kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"Account\"] },\n    }).success).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects empty name\", () => {\n    expect(createSourceSchema.safeParse({ name: \"\", kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] } }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects name over 80 chars\", () => {\n    expect(createSourceSchema.safeParse({ name: \"a\".repeat(81), kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] } }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects an unknown kind\", () => {\n    expect(createSourceSchema.safeParse({ name: \"A\", kind: \"airtable\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] } }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects config.objects being empty (min 1)\", () => {\n    expect(sourceConfigSchema.safeParse({ objects: [] }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"accepts config without the optional filter\", () => {\n    expect(sourceConfigSchema.safeParse({ objects: [\"Account\"] }).success).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// types/conflict.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { severitySchema, conflictSchema } from \"./conflict\";\n\ndescribe(\"severitySchema\", () => {\n  it.each([1, 2, 3, 4])(\"accepts %i\", (v) => expect(severitySchema.safeParse(v).success).toBe(true));\n  it.each([0, 5, 1.5, \"3\", null])(\"rejects %p\", (v) => expect(severitySchema.safeParse(v).success).toBe(false));\n});\n\ndescribe(\"conflictSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects a non-uuid id\", () => {\n    expect(conflictSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"not-a-uuid\", runId: crypto.randomUUID(), matchId: crypto.randomUUID(),\n      field: \"name\", valueA: \"a\", valueB: \"b\",\n      conflictClass: \"attribute\", severity: 3, detectedBy: \"rule\",\n    }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "5. Components — currently zero rendered/interaction tests",
        "content": "\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "`components/severity-mark.tsx` — the one place AGENTS.md explicitly forbids color-only signaling",
        "content": "This is a correctness-critical accessibility contract worth locking in with a test, not just a code comment.\n\n```tsx\n// components/severity-mark.test.tsx\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { SeverityMark } from \"./severity-mark\";\n\ndescribe(\"SeverityMark\", () => {\n  it.each([\n    [4, \"Structural\"], [3, \"Attribute\"], [2, \"Attribute\"], [1, \"Cosmetic\"],\n  ])(\"severity %i always renders its word label, not just the mark\", (severity, label) => {\n    render(<SeverityMark severity={severity as 1 | 2 | 3 | 4} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(label)).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n\n  it(\"renders distinct glyphs for adjacent severities (3 vs 2 collide on label only)\", () => {\n    const { container: c3 } = render(<SeverityMark severity={3} />);\n    const { container: c2 } = render(<SeverityMark severity={2} />);\n    expect(c3.textContent).not.toBe(c2.textContent);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n",
        "level": 4
      },
      {
        "title": "`components/sources/source-table.tsx`",
        "content": "**Gaps:** empty `sources` array (renders header, no rows — no explicit empty-state test exists), multiple `objects` join formatting, unknown `kind` value (TS would catch, but a runtime prop from an untrusted boundary wouldn't — `SOURCE_KIND_LABEL[source.kind]` would render `undefined`).\n\n```tsx\n// components/sources/source-table.test.tsx\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { SourceTable } from \"./source-table\";\nimport type { Source } from \"@/types/source\";\n\nconst source = (overrides: Partial<Source> = {}): Source => ({\n  id: crypto.randomUUID(), name: \"SFDC\", kind: \"salesforce\",\n  config: { objects: [\"Account\", \"Contact\"] }, createdAt: new Date(), ...overrides,\n});\n\ndescribe(\"SourceTable\", () => {\n  it(\"renders a row per source with joined object names\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[source()]} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"SFDC\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Account, Contact\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Salesforce\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"crm\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n\n  it(\"renders only the header row when sources is empty\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[]} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Name\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.queryAllByRole(\"row\")).toHaveLength(1); // header only\n  });\n\n  it(\"renders one row per source across multiple entries with distinct kinds\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[source({ id: \"1\" }), source({ id: \"2\", kind: \"databricks\" })]} />);\n    expect(screen.getAllByRole(\"row\")).toHaveLength(3); // header + 2\n  });\n});\n```\n\n",
        "level": 4
      },
      {
        "title": "`components/console/nav-rail.tsx` — client component with real branching logic",
        "content": "**Gaps:** active-link highlighting via `pathname.startsWith`, loading state (`isLoaded` false → blank label vs. populated), nested route still marks parent active (e.g. `/sources/new` → Sources active). Needs `next/navigation` and `@clerk/nextjs` mocked.\n\n```tsx\n// components/console/nav-rail.test.tsx\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport { NavRail } from \"./nav-rail\";\n\nvi.mock(\"next/navigation\", () => ({ usePathname: () => \"/sources/new\" }));\nvi.mock(\"@clerk/nextjs\", () => ({\n  UserButton: () => <div data-testid=\"user-button\" />,\n  useUser: () => ({ user: { username: \"j.rao\" }, isLoaded: true }),\n}));\nvi.mock(\"@/components/auth/sign-out-control\", () => ({ SignOutControl: () => <button>Sign out</button> }));\n\ndescribe(\"NavRail\", () => {\n  it(\"marks Sources active for a nested route like /sources/new\", () => {\n    render(<NavRail />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Sources\")).toHaveAttribute(\"aria-current\", \"page\");\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Runs\")).not.toHaveAttribute(\"aria-current\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"renders empty reviewer label while Clerk user is still loading\", () => {\n    vi.doMock(\"@clerk/nextjs\", () => ({\n      UserButton: () => <div />,\n      useUser: () => ({ user: null, isLoaded: false }),\n    }));\n    // re-import after doMock in an isolated test file/module reset in real setup\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 4
      },
      {
        "title": "6. Server Component / page-level integration gaps — none exist today",
        "content": "\n`app/(console)/sources/page.tsx` is the one place that branches on `sources.length` to choose empty-state vs. table — this exact boundary (0, 1, many) is untested.\n\n```tsx\n// app/(console)/sources/page.test.tsx\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport SourcesPage from \"./page\";\nimport { listSources } from \"@/lib/server/sources\";\n\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/sources\", () => ({ listSources: vi.fn() }));\n\ndescribe(\"SourcesPage\", () => {\n  it(\"shows the empty state and no 'Add source' header action when there are no sources\", async () => {\n    (listSources as any).mockResolvedValue([]);\n    render(await SourcesPage());\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"No sources yet\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.queryByText(\"Add source\")).not.toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n\n  it(\"shows the table and header count + action once sources exist\", async () => {\n    (listSources as any).mockResolvedValue([{ id: \"1\", name: \"A\", kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] }, createdAt: new Date() }]);\n    render(await SourcesPage());\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"1 configured\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.getAllByText(\"Add source\").length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "7. `proxy.ts` (Clerk middleware) — auth boundary, zero coverage, high blast radius",
        "content": "\nThis is the entire perimeter for an internal tool that renders org charts and mutates the audit trail — a regression here is a data-exposure bug, not a UI bug.\n\n**Gaps:** which routes `isPublicRoute` treats as public vs. protected, and that `auth.protect()` is actually invoked for non-public routes.\n\n```ts\n// proxy.test.ts — test the exported matcher logic directly via createRouteMatcher\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { createRouteMatcher } from \"@clerk/nextjs/server\";\n\nconst isPublicRoute = createRouteMatcher([\"/\", \"/sign-in(.*)\", \"/sign-up(.*)\"]);\n\nfunction req(path: string) {\n  return { nextUrl: { pathname: path } } as any;\n}\n\ndescribe(\"isPublicRoute\", () => {\n  it.each([\"/\", \"/sign-in\", \"/sign-in/factor-one\", \"/sign-up\"])(\"%s is public\", (p) => {\n    expect(isPublicRoute(req(p))).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it.each([\"/runs\", \"/sources\", \"/conflicts\", \"/api/runs\", \"/rules/edit\"])(\"%s requires auth\", (p) => {\n    expect(isPublicRoute(req(p))).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"does not treat /sign-in-like as public via prefix confusion\", () => {\n    // guards against a future regex change loosening the matcher\n    expect(isPublicRoute(req(\"/sign-in-oops\"))).toBe(true); // documents current (.*) behavior — flag if unintended\n  });\n});\n```\n> That last case is worth keeping even though it currently passes — it documents that `/sign-in(.*)` is a prefix match, which is a real footgun if someone ever adds a route like `/sign-in-review-queue`.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Summary of gaps by category",
        "content": "| Category | Files affected | Priority |\n|---|---|---|\n| No test framework installed | whole repo | **Blocker** — nothing below can run until this lands |\n| Pure logic untested | `reviewer-label.ts`, `cn.ts` | High — cheap, high-value |\n| Auth/session branching untested | `lib/server/auth.ts`, `proxy.ts` | High — security boundary |\n| Data access untested | `lib/server/sources.ts` | High — DB row → schema drift is silent today |\n| Schema contracts untested | `types/*.ts` | Medium — mirrors external engine, drift risk |\n| Component logic untested | `severity-mark.tsx`, `source-table.tsx`, `nav-rail.tsx` | Medium |\n| Page-level branching untested | `app/(console)/sources/page.tsx` | Medium |\n| Missing error-handling tests | `requireReviewer` throw path, `getDb()` missing `DATABASE_URL`, `sourceSchema.parse` failure | High — these are the only explicit `throw`s in the codebase and none are exercised |\n| Integration gaps | Any full request → middleware → page → DB flow (e.g. signed-out user hitting `/sources`) | Not yet feasible without a DB/Clerk test harness — recommend Playwright once framework lands |\n\nNext step, if you want it: I can scaffold the actual `vitest.config.ts`, `test/setup.ts` (jsdom + jest-dom matchers), and wire an `npm test` script so these skeletons run as-is.",
        "level": 3
      }
